        "SC09ExactSharesOverflowExploit.test_exploit_fuzzFindsTruncation"
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "SC09ExactSharesOverflowRegression.test_regression_wrappedShareCountReverts",
        "SC09ExactSharesOverflowRegression.test_regression_overflowIsFlagged",
        "SC09ExactSharesOverflowRegression.testFuzz_regression_successfulShiftIsReversible"
      ],
      "signals": [
        { "tool": "foundryInvariant", "id": "invariant_joinsPayProRata" },
        { "tool": "medusa", "id": "property_joinsPayProRata" },
        { "tool": "halmos", "id": "check_checkedShlIsLossless" },
        { "tool": "halmos", "id": "check_checkedShlFullWord" }
      ],
      "triage": "Foundry's shrunk counterexample joins with exactly 2**128 shares (the Q128 constant in the bytecode dictionary) and the recorded Medusa run with about 2**151; both pass the top-64-bit guard, wrap the Q128 ratio and pay a few wei. Halmos models a value just below 2**192 shifted by 65 bits, and the same value shifted by a full word."
